IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc6-builders`

-- ccc6-children.l4 -- ss 169.1 (Recruitment of a young person), 170 (Parent or guardian procuring sexual activity), 171 (Householder permitting prohibited sexual activity),
-- 171.1 (Making sexually explicit material available to a child), 172 (Corrupting children), 172.1 (Luring a child) and 172.2 (Agreement or arrangement: sexual offence against a child).
-- (s 173 is in ccc6-disorderly.l4.) An offence function answers JUST TRUE when every element is met and NOTHING otherwise (fork F1); a bar ("it is not a defence ... unless") answers JUST TRUE when it applies,
-- JUST FALSE when its "unless" is met and NOTHING when the case is outside it (forks F2, F4). Where a section says "guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction" and states no penalty, s 787(1) is an input (another part).
-- NOT is always written on a line of its own or in brackets: on the stable binary `NOT (x) AND y` on one line reads as NOT (x AND y).

§ `s 169.1 Recruitment — young person`

-- src:3391 | Definition of young person
-- src:3392 | (5) In this section, young person means a person under the age of 18 years.
@ref Criminal Code s 169.1(5) (src:3391-3392)
GIVEN `the age of the person in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 169.1(5) young person` MEANS
    IF `the age of the person in years` LESS THAN 18
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "young person means a person under the age of 18 years"

-- (2) "a person is considered to be in a position of trust, power or authority towards a young person by reason, among others, of being 18 years of age or more": "among others" leaves the reasons open.
-- src:3383 | Position of trust, power or authority
-- src:3384 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), a person is considered to be in a position of trust, power or authority towards a young person by reason, among others, of being 18 years of age or more.
@ref Criminal Code s 169.1(2) (src:3383-3384)
GIVEN `the age of the person in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 169.1(2) the person is considered to be in a position of trust, power or authority towards the young person` MEANS
    IF `the age of the person in years` AT LEAST 18
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "by reason, among others, of being 18 years of age or more"

DECLARE `s 169.1(1) what the person did` IS ONE OF
    `s 169.1(1) recruits`
    `s 169.1(1) counsels`
    `s 169.1(1) encourages`
    `s 169.1(1) invites`
    `s 169.1(1) none of those`

-- src:3381 | Recruitment — young person
-- src:3382 | 169.1 (1) Every person is guilty of an offence who — being in a position of trust, power or authority towards a young person and knowing that the young person is under 18 years of age or being reckless as to that fact — recruits, counsels, encourages or invites the young person to be a party to an offence under this Act or the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act if the young person is afterwards a party to that offence or an offence related to that offence.
@ref Criminal Code s 169.1(1) (src:3381-3382)
GIVEN `s 169.1(5) young person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 169.1(2) the person is considered to be in a position of trust, power or authority towards the young person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is in a position of trust, power or authority towards the young person for another reason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knew that the young person is under 18 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was reckless as to the young person's being under 18 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the person did` IS A `s 169.1(1) what the person did`
      `it was to be a party to an offence under this Act or the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the young person is afterwards a party to that offence or an offence related to that offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 169.1(1) the conduct is the offence of recruiting a young person to an offence` MEANS
    IF    `s 169.1(5) young person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND (   `s 169.1(2) the person is considered to be in a position of trust, power or authority towards the young person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `the person is in a position of trust, power or authority towards the young person for another reason`)
      AND (   `the person knew that the young person is under 18 years of age`
           OR `the person was reckless as to the young person's being under 18 years of age`)
      AND NOT (`what the person did` EQUALS `s 169.1(1) none of those`)
      AND `it was to be a party to an offence under this Act or the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act`
      AND `the young person is afterwards a party to that offence or an offence related to that offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person is guilty of an offence who — being in a position of trust, power or authority towards a young person and knowing that the young person is under 18 years of age or being reckless as to that fact — recruits, counsels, encourages or invites the young person to be a party to an offence under this Act or the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act if the young person is afterwards a party to that offence or an offence related to that offence"

-- src:3385 | No defence
-- src:3386 | (3) It is not a defence to a charge under subsection (1) that the accused believed that the young person was at least 18 years of age unless the accused took reasonable steps to ascertain the age of the young person.
@ref Criminal Code s 169.1(3) (src:3385-3386)
GIVEN `the accused believed that the young person was at least 18 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused took reasonable steps to ascertain the age of the young person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 169.1(3) the belief that the young person was at least 18 is not a defence: the bar applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused believed that the young person was at least 18 years of age`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is not a defence to a charge under subsection (1) that the accused believed that the young person was at least 18 years of age"
        IF `the accused took reasonable steps to ascertain the age of the young person`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the accused took reasonable steps to ascertain the age of the young person"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:3387 | Punishment
-- src:3388 | (4) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1) is
-- src:3389 | (a) guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:3390 | (b) guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 169.1(4) (src:3387-3390)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 169.1(4)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 169.1(4)(b) (src:3390)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 169.1(4)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `ss 150 to 182 the punishment on summary conviction that s 787(1) fixes` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 169.1(4) (src:3387-3390)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 169.1 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

§ `s 170 Parent or guardian procuring sexual activity`

-- src:3393 | Parent or guardian procuring sexual activity
-- src:3394 | 170 Every parent or guardian of a person under the age of 18 years who procures the person for the purpose of engaging in any sexual activity prohibited by this Act with a person other than the parent or guardian is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of one year.
@ref Criminal Code s 170 (src:3393-3394)
GIVEN `the person is a parent of the person procured` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 150 guardian: the person is a guardian of the person procured` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the age in years of the person procured` IS A NUMBER
      `the person procured the other person for the purpose of engaging in sexual activity prohibited by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sexual activity is with a person other than the parent or guardian` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 170 the conduct is the offence of a parent or guardian procuring a person under 18 for sexual activity` MEANS
    IF    (`the person is a parent of the person procured` OR `s 150 guardian: the person is a guardian of the person procured` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
      AND `the age in years of the person procured` LESS THAN 18
      AND `the person procured the other person for the purpose of engaging in sexual activity prohibited by this Act`
      AND `the sexual activity is with a person other than the parent or guardian`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every parent or guardian of a person under the age of 18 years who procures the person for the purpose of engaging in any sexual activity prohibited by this Act with a person other than the parent or guardian is guilty of an indictable offence"

@ref Criminal Code s 170 (src:3394)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 170 the punishment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 170 (src:3394)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 170 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

§ `s 171 Householder permitting prohibited sexual activity`

-- src:3395 | Householder permitting prohibited sexual activity
-- src:3396 | 171 Every owner, occupier or manager of premises, or any other person who has control of premises or assists in the management or control of premises, who knowingly permits a person under the age of 18 years to resort to or to be in or on the premises for the purpose of engaging in any sexual activity prohibited by this Act is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of one year.
@ref Criminal Code s 171 (src:3395-3396)
GIVEN `the person is an owner, occupier or manager of the premises, or another person who has control of the premises or assists in the management or control of the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly permitted the other person to resort to or to be in or on the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the age in years of the other person` IS A NUMBER
      `it was for the purpose of engaging in sexual activity prohibited by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171 the conduct is the offence of a householder permitting prohibited sexual activity` MEANS
    IF    `the person is an owner, occupier or manager of the premises, or another person who has control of the premises or assists in the management or control of the premises`
      AND `the person knowingly permitted the other person to resort to or to be in or on the premises`
      AND `the age in years of the other person` LESS THAN 18
      AND `it was for the purpose of engaging in sexual activity prohibited by this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every owner, occupier or manager of premises, or any other person who has control of premises or assists in the management or control of premises, who knowingly permits a person under the age of 18 years to resort to or to be in or on the premises for the purpose of engaging in any sexual activity prohibited by this Act is guilty of an indictable offence"

@ref Criminal Code s 171 (src:3396)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 171 the punishment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 171 (src:3396)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 171 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

§ `s 171.1 Making sexually explicit material available to child`

-- The three lists of offences the accused may be facilitating, by section number (R1); the same lists are used by ss 172.1 and 172.2.
-- src:3397 | Making sexually explicit material available to child
-- src:3398 | 171.1 (1) Every person commits an offence who transmits, makes available, distributes or sells sexually explicit material to
-- src:3399 | (a) a person who is, or who the accused believes is, under the age of 18 years, for the purpose of facilitating the commission of an offence with respect to that person under subsection 153(1), section 155, 163.1, 170, 171 or 279.011 or subsection 279.02(2), 279.03(2), 286.1(2), 286.2(2) or 286.3(2);
-- src:3400 | (b) a person who is, or who the accused believes is, under the age of 16 years, for the purpose of facilitating the commission of an offence under section 151 or 152, subsection 160(3) or 173(2) or section 271, 272, 273 or 280 with respect to that person; or
-- src:3401 | (c) a person who is, or who the accused believes is, under the age of 14 years, for the purpose of facilitating the commission of an offence under section 281 with respect to that person.
@ref Criminal Code s 171.1(1) (src:3397-3401)
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 171.1(1)(a) the offence is one under subsection 153(1), section 155, 163.1, 170, 171 or 279.011 or subsection 279.02(2), 279.03(2), 286.1(2), 286.2(2) or 286.3(2)` MEANS
       `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` `the offence` 153 "(1)"
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence` 155
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence` 163.1
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence` 170
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence` 171
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence` 279.011
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` `the offence` 279.02 "(2)"
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` `the offence` 279.03 "(2)"
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` `the offence` 286.1 "(2)"
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` `the offence` 286.2 "(2)"
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` `the offence` 286.3 "(2)"

@ref Criminal Code s 171.1(1) (src:3397-3401)
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 171.1(1)(b) the offence is one under section 151 or 152, subsection 160(3) or 173(2) or section 271, 272, 273 or 280` MEANS
       `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence` 151
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence` 152
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` `the offence` 160 "(3)"
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` `the offence` 173 "(2)"
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence` 271
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence` 272
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence` 273
    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence` 280

@ref Criminal Code s 171.1(1) (src:3397-3401)
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 171.1(1)(c) the offence is one under section 281` MEANS
    `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the offence` 281

-- "a person who is, or who the accused believes is, under the age of N years".
@ref Criminal Code s 171.1(1) (src:3397-3401)
GIVEN `the actual age of the person in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the age the accused believes the person to be, in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the age limit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 171.1(1) the person is, or the accused believes the person is, under the age` MEANS
    `the actual age of the person in years` LESS THAN `the age limit` OR `the age the accused believes the person to be, in years` LESS THAN `the age limit`

DECLARE `s 171.1(1) what the person did` IS ONE OF
    `s 171.1(1) transmits`
    `s 171.1(1) makes available`
    `s 171.1(1) distributes`
    `s 171.1(1) sells`
    `s 171.1(1) none of those`

@ref Criminal Code s 171.1(1) (src:3397-3401)
GIVEN `what the person did` IS A `s 171.1(1) what the person did`
      `s 171.1(5) sexually explicit material` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the actual age of the person in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the age the accused believes the person to be, in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the offence the accused meant to facilitate` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `it was for the purpose of facilitating the commission of that offence with respect to that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171.1(1) the conduct is the offence of making sexually explicit material available to a child` MEANS
    IF    NOT (`what the person did` EQUALS `s 171.1(1) none of those`)
      AND `s 171.1(5) sexually explicit material` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND `it was for the purpose of facilitating the commission of that offence with respect to that person`
      AND (   (   `s 171.1(1) the person is, or the accused believes the person is, under the age` `the actual age of the person in years` `the age the accused believes the person to be, in years` 18
              AND `s 171.1(1)(a) the offence is one under subsection 153(1), section 155, 163.1, 170, 171 or 279.011 or subsection 279.02(2), 279.03(2), 286.1(2), 286.2(2) or 286.3(2)` `the offence the accused meant to facilitate`)
           OR (   `s 171.1(1) the person is, or the accused believes the person is, under the age` `the actual age of the person in years` `the age the accused believes the person to be, in years` 16
              AND `s 171.1(1)(b) the offence is one under section 151 or 152, subsection 160(3) or 173(2) or section 271, 272, 273 or 280` `the offence the accused meant to facilitate`)
           OR (   `s 171.1(1) the person is, or the accused believes the person is, under the age` `the actual age of the person in years` `the age the accused believes the person to be, in years` 14
              AND `s 171.1(1)(c) the offence is one under section 281` `the offence the accused meant to facilitate`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person commits an offence who transmits, makes available, distributes or sells sexually explicit material to (a) a person who is, or who the accused believes is, under the age of 18 years, for the purpose of facilitating the commission of an offence ... (b) ... under the age of 16 years ... (c) ... under the age of 14 years, for the purpose of facilitating the commission of an offence under section 281 with respect to that person"

-- (5) sexually explicit material (read by (1) above).
-- src:3410 | Definition of sexually explicit material
-- src:3411 | (5) In subsection (1), sexually explicit material means material that is not child sexual abuse and exploitation material, as defined in subsection 163.1(1), and that is
-- src:3412 | (a) a photographic, film, video or other visual representation, whether or not it was made by electronic or mechanical means,
-- src:3413 | (i) that shows a person who is engaged in or is depicted as engaged in explicit sexual activity, or
-- src:3414 | (ii) the dominant characteristic of which is the depiction, for a sexual purpose, of a person’s sexual organs;
-- src:3415 | (b) written material whose dominant characteristic is the description, for a sexual purpose, of explicit sexual activity involving a person; or
-- src:3416 | (c) an audio recording whose dominant characteristic is the description, presentation or representation, for a sexual purpose, of explicit sexual activity involving a person.
@ref Criminal Code s 171.1(5) (src:3410-3416)
GIVEN `s 163.1(1) child sexual abuse and exploitation material` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is a photographic, film, video or other visual representation, whether or not it was made by electronic or mechanical means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it shows a person who is engaged in or is depicted as engaged in explicit sexual activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a dominant characteristic of the visual representation is the depiction, for a sexual purpose, of a person's sexual organs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is written material whose dominant characteristic is the description, for a sexual purpose, of explicit sexual activity involving a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an audio recording whose dominant characteristic is the description, presentation or representation, for a sexual purpose, of explicit sexual activity involving a person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171.1(5) sexually explicit material` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 163.1(1) child sexual abuse and exploitation material` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "sexually explicit material means material that is not child sexual abuse and exploitation material, as defined in subsection 163.1(1)"
        IF `s 163.1(1) child sexual abuse and exploitation material` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the material is child sexual abuse and exploitation material (s 163.1(1)) was not answered
        IF    (   `it is a photographic, film, video or other visual representation, whether or not it was made by electronic or mechanical means`
              AND (   `it shows a person who is engaged in or is depicted as engaged in explicit sexual activity`
                   OR `a dominant characteristic of the visual representation is the depiction, for a sexual purpose, of a person's sexual organs`))
           OR `it is written material whose dominant characteristic is the description, for a sexual purpose, of explicit sexual activity involving a person`
           OR `it is an audio recording whose dominant characteristic is the description, presentation or representation, for a sexual purpose, of explicit sexual activity involving a person`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "sexually explicit material means material that is not child sexual abuse and exploitation material ... and that is (a) a photographic, film, video or other visual representation ... (b) written material ... or (c) an audio recording"

-- src:3402 | Punishment
-- src:3403 | (2) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1)
-- src:3404 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of six months; or
-- src:3405 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of 90 days.
@ref Criminal Code s 171.1(2) (src:3402-3405)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 171.1(2)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `imprisonment for a term of` `six months`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 171.1(2)(b) (src:3405)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 171.1(2)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ninety days`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 171.1(2) (src:3402-3405)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 171.1 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- (3) "Evidence that the person ... was represented to the accused as being under the age of 18, 16 or 14 years, as the case may be, is, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, proof that the accused believed that the person was under that age."
-- src:3406 | Presumption
-- src:3407 | (3) Evidence that the person referred to in paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c) was represented to the accused as being under the age of 18, 16 or 14 years, as the case may be, is, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, proof that the accused believed that the person was under that age.
@ref Criminal Code s 171.1(3) (src:3406-3407)
GIVEN `the person was represented to the accused as being under the age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171.1(3) the evidence is proof that the accused believed that the person was under that age` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person was represented to the accused as being under the age` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Evidence that the person ... was represented to the accused as being under the age of 18, 16 or 14 years"
        IF `there is evidence to the contrary` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of evidence to the contrary"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:3408 | No defence
-- src:3409 | (4) It is not a defence to a charge under paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c) that the accused believed that the person referred to in that paragraph was at least 18, 16 or 14 years of age, as the case may be, unless the accused took reasonable steps to ascertain the age of the person.
@ref Criminal Code s 171.1(4) (src:3408-3409)
GIVEN `the charge is under paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c) and the accused believed that the person was at least 18, 16 or 14 years of age, as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused took reasonable steps to ascertain the age of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171.1(4) the belief that the person was at least the age is not a defence: the bar applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the charge is under paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c) and the accused believed that the person was at least 18, 16 or 14 years of age, as the case may be`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is not a defence to a charge under paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c) that the accused believed that the person referred to in that paragraph was at least 18, 16 or 14 years of age, as the case may be"
        IF `the accused took reasonable steps to ascertain the age of the person`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the accused took reasonable steps to ascertain the age of the person"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (6) "For greater certainty, a reference to sexual activity in subsection (5) includes a reference to an act of bestiality, as defined in subsection 160(7)."
-- src:3417 | For greater certainty
-- src:3418 | (6) For greater certainty, a reference to sexual activity in subsection (5) includes a reference to an act of bestiality, as defined in subsection 160(7).
@ref Criminal Code s 171.1(6) (src:3417-3418)
GIVEN `s 160(7) bestiality` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171.1(6) the activity is sexual activity for the purposes of subsection (5)` MEANS
    IF `s 160(7) bestiality` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a reference to sexual activity in subsection (5) includes a reference to an act of bestiality"

§ `s 172 Corrupting children`

-- src:3425 | (3) For the purposes of this section, child means a person who is or appears to be under the age of eighteen years.
@ref Criminal Code s 172(3) (src:3425)
GIVEN `the age of the person in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the person appears to be under the age of eighteen years` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 172(3) child` MEANS
    IF `the age of the person in years` LESS THAN 18 OR `the person appears to be under the age of eighteen years`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "child means a person who is or appears to be under the age of eighteen years"

DECLARE `s 172(1) what the person did` IS ONE OF
    `s 172(1) participates in adultery`
    `s 172(1) participates in sexual immorality`
    `s 172(1) indulges in habitual drunkenness`
    `s 172(1) indulges in another form of vice`
    `s 172(1) none of those`

-- src:3419 | Corrupting children
-- src:3420 | 172 (1) Every person who, in the home of a child, participates in adultery or sexual immorality or indulges in habitual drunkenness or any other form of vice, and by doing so endangers the morals of the child or renders the home an unfit place for the child to be in, is guilty of
-- src:3421 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:3422 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 172(1) (src:3419-3422)
GIVEN `the person did it in the home of a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 172(3) child` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `what the person did` IS A `s 172(1) what the person did`
      `by doing so the person endangers the morals of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by doing so the person renders the home an unfit place for the child to be in` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 172(1) the conduct is the offence of corrupting children` MEANS
    IF    `the person did it in the home of a child`
      AND `s 172(3) child` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND NOT (`what the person did` EQUALS `s 172(1) none of those`)
      AND (   `by doing so the person endangers the morals of the child`
           OR `by doing so the person renders the home an unfit place for the child to be in`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who, in the home of a child, participates in adultery or sexual immorality or indulges in habitual drunkenness or any other form of vice, and by doing so endangers the morals of the child or renders the home an unfit place for the child to be in, is guilty of"

@ref Criminal Code s 172(1)(a) (src:3421)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 172(1)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 172(1)(b) (src:3422)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 172(1)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `ss 150 to 182 the punishment on summary conviction that s 787(1) fixes` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 172(1) (src:3419-3422)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 172 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- (4) "No proceedings shall be commenced under subsection (1) without the consent of the Attorney General, unless they are instituted by or at the instance of a recognized society for the protection of children or by an officer of a juvenile court."
-- src:3426 | Who may institute prosecutions
-- src:3427 | (4) No proceedings shall be commenced under subsection (1) without the consent of the Attorney General, unless they are instituted by or at the instance of a recognized society for the protection of children or by an officer of a juvenile court.
@ref Criminal Code s 172(4) (src:3426-3427)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General has consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are instituted by or at the instance of a recognized society for the protection of children or by an officer of a juvenile court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 172(4) no proceedings shall be commenced without the consent of the Attorney General: the bar applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the proceedings are proceedings under subsection (1)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No proceedings shall be commenced under subsection (1)"
        IF `the Attorney General has consented` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "without the consent of the Attorney General"
        IF `the proceedings are instituted by or at the instance of a recognized society for the protection of children or by an officer of a juvenile court` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless they are instituted by or at the instance of a recognized society for the protection of children or by an officer of a juvenile court"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `s 172.1 Luring a child`

DECLARE `s 172.1(1) the person's offence of a sexual nature` IS ONE OF
    `s 172.1(1)(a) an offence under section 346 of a sexual nature or for a sexual purpose`
    `s 172.1(1)(a) an offence under section 346 that is neither of a sexual nature nor for a sexual purpose`
    `s 172.1(1)(a) another offence`

-- src:3428 | Luring a child
-- src:3429 | 172.1 (1) Every person commits an offence who, by a means of telecommunication, communicates with
-- src:3430 | (a) a person who is, or who the accused believes is, under the age of 18 years, for the purpose of facilitating the commission of an offence with respect to that person under subsection 153(1), section 155, 163.1, 170, 171 or 279.011 or subsection 279.02(2), 279.03(2), 286.1(2), 286.2(2) or 286.3(2) or the commission of an offence with respect to that person under section 346 of a sexual nature or for a sexual purpose;
-- src:3431 | (b) a person who is, or who the accused believes is, under the age of 16 years, for the purpose of facilitating the commission of an offence under section 151 or 152, subsection 160(3) or 173(2) or section 271, 272, 273 or 280 with respect to that person; or
-- src:3432 | (c) a person who is, or who the accused believes is, under the age of 14 years, for the purpose of facilitating the commission of an offence under section 281 with respect to that person.
@ref Criminal Code s 172.1(1) (src:3428-3432)
GIVEN `the person communicated by a means of telecommunication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the actual age of the person communicated with, in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the age the accused believes the person to be, in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the offence the accused meant to facilitate` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `whether the offence is one under section 346` IS A `s 172.1(1) the person's offence of a sexual nature`
      `it was for the purpose of facilitating the commission of that offence with respect to that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 172.1(1) the conduct is the offence of luring a child` MEANS
    IF    `the person communicated by a means of telecommunication`
      AND `it was for the purpose of facilitating the commission of that offence with respect to that person`
      AND (   (   `s 171.1(1) the person is, or the accused believes the person is, under the age` `the actual age of the person communicated with, in years` `the age the accused believes the person to be, in years` 18
              AND (   `s 171.1(1)(a) the offence is one under subsection 153(1), section 155, 163.1, 170, 171 or 279.011 or subsection 279.02(2), 279.03(2), 286.1(2), 286.2(2) or 286.3(2)` `the offence the accused meant to facilitate`
                   OR `whether the offence is one under section 346` EQUALS `s 172.1(1)(a) an offence under section 346 of a sexual nature or for a sexual purpose`))
           OR (   `s 171.1(1) the person is, or the accused believes the person is, under the age` `the actual age of the person communicated with, in years` `the age the accused believes the person to be, in years` 16
              AND `s 171.1(1)(b) the offence is one under section 151 or 152, subsection 160(3) or 173(2) or section 271, 272, 273 or 280` `the offence the accused meant to facilitate`)
           OR (   `s 171.1(1) the person is, or the accused believes the person is, under the age` `the actual age of the person communicated with, in years` `the age the accused believes the person to be, in years` 14
              AND `s 171.1(1)(c) the offence is one under section 281` `the offence the accused meant to facilitate`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person commits an offence who, by a means of telecommunication, communicates with (a) a person who is, or who the accused believes is, under the age of 18 years, for the purpose of facilitating the commission of an offence with respect to that person under subsection 153(1), section 155, 163.1, 170, 171 or 279.011 or subsection 279.02(2), 279.03(2), 286.1(2), 286.2(2) or 286.3(2) or the commission of an offence with respect to that person under section 346 of a sexual nature or for a sexual purpose; (b) ... under the age of 16 years ... (c) ... under the age of 14 years"

-- src:3433 | Punishment
-- src:3434 | (2) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1)
-- src:3435 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of one year; or
-- src:3436 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of six months.
