GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 172.1 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:3437 | Presumption re age
-- src:3438 | (3) Evidence that the person referred to in paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c) was represented to the accused as being under the age of eighteen years, sixteen years or fourteen years, as the case may be, is, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, proof that the accused believed that the person was under that age.
@ref Criminal Code s 172.1(3) (src:3437-3438)
GIVEN `the person was represented to the accused as being under the age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 172.1(3) the evidence is proof that the accused believed that the person was under that age` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person was represented to the accused as being under the age` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Evidence that the person referred to in paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c) was represented to the accused as being under the age of eighteen years, sixteen years or fourteen years"
        IF `there is evidence to the contrary` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of evidence to the contrary"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:3439 | No defence
-- src:3440 | (4) It is not a defence to a charge under paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c) that the accused believed that the person referred to in that paragraph was at least eighteen years of age, sixteen years or fourteen years of age, as the case may be, unless the accused took reasonable steps to ascertain the age of the person.
@ref Criminal Code s 172.1(4) (src:3439-3440)
GIVEN `the charge is under paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c) and the accused believed that the person was at least eighteen years of age, sixteen years or fourteen years of age, as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused took reasonable steps to ascertain the age of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 172.1(4) the belief that the person was at least the age is not a defence: the bar applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the charge is under paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c) and the accused believed that the person was at least eighteen years of age, sixteen years or fourteen years of age, as the case may be`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is not a defence to a charge under paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c) that the accused believed that the person referred to in that paragraph was at least eighteen years of age, sixteen years or fourteen years of age, as the case may be"
        IF `the accused took reasonable steps to ascertain the age of the person`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the accused took reasonable steps to ascertain the age of the person"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `s 172.2 Agreement or arrangement — sexual offence against child`

-- src:3443 | Agreement or arrangement — sexual offence against child
-- src:3444 | 172.2 (1) Every person commits an offence who, by a means of telecommunication, agrees with a person, or makes an arrangement with a person, to commit an offence
-- src:3445 | (a) under subsection 153(1), section 155, 163.1, 170, 171 or 279.011 or subsection 279.02(2), 279.03(2), 286.1(2), 286.2(2) or 286.3(2) with respect to another person who is, or who the accused believes is, under the age of 18 years;
-- src:3446 | (b) under section 151 or 152, subsection 160(3) or 173(2) or section 271, 272, 273 or 280 with respect to another person who is, or who the accused believes is, under the age of 16 years; or
-- src:3447 | (c) under section 281 with respect to another person who is, or who the accused believes is, under the age of 14 years.
@ref Criminal Code s 172.2(1) (src:3443-3447)
GIVEN `the person agreed with another person, or made an arrangement with another person, by a means of telecommunication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence they agreed or arranged to commit` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the actual age of the other person with respect to whom it is to be committed, in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the age the accused believes that other person to be, in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 172.2(1) the conduct is the offence of agreeing or arranging to commit a sexual offence against a child` MEANS
    IF    `the person agreed with another person, or made an arrangement with another person, by a means of telecommunication`
      AND (   (   `s 171.1(1) the person is, or the accused believes the person is, under the age` `the actual age of the other person with respect to whom it is to be committed, in years` `the age the accused believes that other person to be, in years` 18
              AND `s 171.1(1)(a) the offence is one under subsection 153(1), section 155, 163.1, 170, 171 or 279.011 or subsection 279.02(2), 279.03(2), 286.1(2), 286.2(2) or 286.3(2)` `the offence they agreed or arranged to commit`)
           OR (   `s 171.1(1) the person is, or the accused believes the person is, under the age` `the actual age of the other person with respect to whom it is to be committed, in years` `the age the accused believes that other person to be, in years` 16
              AND `s 171.1(1)(b) the offence is one under section 151 or 152, subsection 160(3) or 173(2) or section 271, 272, 273 or 280` `the offence they agreed or arranged to commit`)
           OR (   `s 171.1(1) the person is, or the accused believes the person is, under the age` `the actual age of the other person with respect to whom it is to be committed, in years` `the age the accused believes that other person to be, in years` 14
              AND `s 171.1(1)(c) the offence is one under section 281` `the offence they agreed or arranged to commit`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person commits an offence who, by a means of telecommunication, agrees with a person, or makes an arrangement with a person, to commit an offence (a) under subsection 153(1), section 155, 163.1, 170, 171 or 279.011 or subsection 279.02(2), 279.03(2), 286.1(2), 286.2(2) or 286.3(2) with respect to another person who is, or who the accused believes is, under the age of 18 years; (b) ... under the age of 16 years; or (c) under section 281 with respect to another person who is, or who the accused believes is, under the age of 14 years"

