-- (5)(a) "that the person with whom the accused agreed or made an arrangement was a peace officer or a person acting under the direction of a peace officer": s 2 "peace officer" is a seam (an input).
-- src:3456 | No defence
-- src:3457 | (5) It is not a defence to a charge under paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c)
-- src:3458 | (a) that the person with whom the accused agreed or made an arrangement was a peace officer or a person acting under the direction of a peace officer; or
-- src:3459 | (b) that, if the person with whom the accused agreed or made an arrangement was a peace officer or a person acting under the direction of a peace officer, the person referred to in paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c) did not exist.
@ref Criminal Code s 172.2(5) (src:3456-3459)
GIVEN `the charge is under paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 peace officer: the person with whom the accused agreed or made an arrangement was a peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person with whom the accused agreed or made an arrangement was a person acting under the direction of a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 172.2(5)(a) it is not a defence that the person with whom the accused agreed was a peace officer or acting under the direction of one` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the charge is under paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is not a defence to a charge under paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c)"
        IF `s 2 peace officer: the person with whom the accused agreed or made an arrangement was a peace officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the person with whom the accused agreed or made an arrangement was a person acting under the direction of a peace officer` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 2 peace officer: the person with whom the accused agreed or made an arrangement was a peace officer` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 2 "peace officer" includes, and its answer was not given
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) that the person with whom the accused agreed or made an arrangement was a peace officer or a person acting under the direction of a peace officer"

@ref Criminal Code s 172.2(5)(b) (src:3459)
GIVEN `the charge is under paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person with whom the accused agreed or made an arrangement was a peace officer or a person acting under the direction of a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person referred to in paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c) did not exist` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 172.2(5)(b) it is not a defence that the person referred to did not exist` MEANS
    IF `the charge is under paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c)` AND `the person with whom the accused agreed or made an arrangement was a peace officer or a person acting under the direction of a peace officer` AND `the person referred to in paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c) did not exist`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) that, if the person with whom the accused agreed or made an arrangement was a peace officer or a person acting under the direction of a peace officer, the person referred to in paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c) did not exist"
